  "contract": [
    "Mode6 allocates984 bytes, returns null before reading weights on allocation failure, clears the allocation, stores type6 and constructs quantizer/aligned/layer/vector/pool records in native order. Its incoming parameter pointer is ignored, including null and unmapped values.",
    "Reusable layer writes176 bytes with five aligned descriptors, a quantizer, optional projection flag/descriptor and pair data. When projection is disabled, the24-byte optional record is untouched. The live configuration group byte at depthwise construction must be nonzero.",
    "Configuration bytes are read in native order at each call site. The projection decision occurs after clearing the flag; enabled projection stores1 then rereads output/input bytes. Overlapping configurations at7e/84/88/a0 demonstrate actual changes in the decision and input dimensions.",
    "Forty readonly layer-configuration bytes match native schema constants. Existing C graph helpers and memory primitives execute, and the merge getter returns one opaque identity data word without assuming a callable executor ABI.",
    "279 direct comparisons execute all768 native instruction bytes with independent complete instance/layer/cursor/field/return oracles and exact configuration/model-header read sequences. Only malloc is modeled. Mode6 consumes exactly6268 model bytes; source cannot execute stock.",
    "128 successful full HR constructor/actual allocator/complete teardown replays call no function ports. Mode0/1/6 graph records allocate through real C code and all primary/workspace/filter/graph/queue/state allocations coalesce to prior heap top. Mode0/1 extents match6660/2979 words; mode6 final model reads are offsets6260/6264 and end at6268, matching1567 words."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This closes ordinary HR initialization graph-function boundaries in the replay, not numerical inference or all firmware hardware dependencies. Fifteen opaque executor identity data imports remain unresolved. Identity words are not callable executor implementations.",
    "Five external fatal/logging/system bindings remain available in the full heap fixture, but successful constructor/teardown paths independently assert zero calls to them. Fatal resource-exhaustion delivery and physical fault behavior are outside this proof.",
    "The direct allocator model now paints only successful allocations; failure cases preserve unallocated payload bytes. Overlap and arbitrary ignored-parameter cases use logical emulator memory, not a physical ownership guarantee.",
    "Live depthwise group byte zero, invalid weights/configuration pointers, concurrency, cold floating-point activation, physical faults, caller scratch and private frames remain unproven. Typed resource-pointer normalization is limited to comparison output; packed scalar words stay exact and actual memory is not rewritten.",
    "The891-unit ld-r composition passes without failures or duplicate strong symbols.880 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged; tested object equals normal object; no writable state added. The40-byte numeric schema is readonly data, not executable bytes.",
    "One mode6 function import is replaced by one deeper opaque merge-executor identity data import, application remains76; boot22. Source-plan/cache layout unchanged. Final executable linking/startup, complete executor/inference code, other sensor engines and hardware boot remain open."
  ],
